  <artifactId>agents-turn</artifactId>
  <name>agents-turn</name>
  <description>
    The chat turn path: AgentChatService and the turn pipeline (agents.turn,
    turn.quality, turn.cache), the chat SSE endpoint (AgentChatStreamController,
    published in the API spec as AgentController), edge routing, memory and
    user memory, context compaction, hooks, the turn journal, resumable
    streams, branching, decisions, the gateway, assist, skills, experiments,
    vision sessions, the load-test allowlist, the collaborator and specialist
    hand-off ports (collab, crew) and public agent shares (share). Split out of
    core/agents by ADR-0023; the Java packages are unchanged.

    Direction: agents-turn depends on agents only. It reaches the tool layer
    through the kernel port tools.AgentToolPort, so it does not depend on
    core/agents-tools; agents-tools depends on agents-turn instead (its
    resolvers delegate to AgentChatService, call the memory and hook services
    and use context compaction). The turn runs in-process in every shape that
    loads this jar (AGENTS.md rule 6): a separate jar, not a network hop.
  </description>

